   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Inaci for your help. This will surely work . Just in case somebody is not being able to view it clearly. Just run &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">plot(env, </span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;resources&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;usage&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">, c(</span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;male&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;female&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;counter&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.05px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">),c(&quot;server&quot;))</span>&quot; . This will give the utilization of number of male and female resources used.<div>Hence giving the queue length as posted in the question.</div><div><br></div><div>Regards,</div><div><br></div><div>Salman Memon</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><div><br>On Wednesday, September 27, 2017 at 3:25:26 AM UTC+5:30, Iñaki Úcar wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">2017-09-26 23:19 GMT+02:00 salman anis &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">1reach...@gmail.com</a>&gt;:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hi,I am starting to use SIMMER. My question might not be very difficult but still please help me out. I have 2 types of arrivals fighting for the same resource. I tried plotting the total queue length using simmer.plot which is working. But how do I plot total number of each arrival type in the queue over the entire time period? Is there any elegant way?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nExample : At a ticket counter there are males and females arriving at a different rate. I am able to plot the total queue length. But how to I plot the total number of males and females in the queue seperately?</blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You can use additional “dumb” resources to account for that. Example:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(simmer)\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(simmer.plot)\r\n\r\nperson &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(sex, lambda)\r\n  trajectory() %&gt;%\r\n  seize(sex) %&gt;%\r\n  seize(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;counter&quot;</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  release(sex) %&gt;%\r\n  timeout(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>() rexp(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>, lambda)) %&gt;%\r\n  release(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;counter&quot;</span>)\r\n\r\nenv &lt;- simmer() %&gt;%\r\n  add_resource(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;counter&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>, <span>Inf</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  add_resource(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;male&quot;</span>, <span>Inf</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  add_generator(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;male&quot;</span>, person(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;male&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>), <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>() rexp(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">100</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>)) %&gt;%\r\n  add_resource(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;female&quot;</span>, <span>Inf</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  add_generator(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;female&quot;</span>, person(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;female&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3</span>), <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>() rexp(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">100</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>)) %&gt;%\r\n  run(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1000</span>)\r\n\r\nplot(env, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;resources&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;usage&quot;</span>, c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;male&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;female&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;counter&quot;</span>))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Regards,<br>Iñaki </p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGksPGJyPjxkaXYgY2xhc3M9ImdtYWlsX2V4dHJhIj48YnI+PGRpdiBjbGFzcz0iZ21haWxfcXVv\r\ndGUiPjIwMTctMDktMjYgMjM6MTkgR01UKzAyOjAwIHNhbG1hbiBhbmlzIDxzcGFuIGRpcj0ibHRy\r\nIj4mbHQ7PGEgaHJlZj0ibWFpbHRvOjFyZWFjaHNhbG1hbkBnbWFpbC5jb20iIHRhcmdldD0iX2Js\r\nYW5rIj4xcmVhY2hzYWxtYW5AZ21haWwuY29tPC9hPiZndDs8L3NwYW4+Ojxicj48YmxvY2txdW90\r\nZSBjbGFzcz0iZ21haWxfcXVvdGUiIHN0eWxlPSJtYXJnaW46IDBweCAwcHggMHB4IDAuOGV4OyBi\r\nb3JkZXItbGVmdDogMXB4IHNvbGlkIHJnYigyMDQsIDIwNCwgMjA0KTsgcGFkZGluZy1sZWZ0OiAx\r\nZXg7Ij5IaSxJIGFtIHN0YXJ0aW5nIHRvIHVzZSBTSU1NRVIuIE15IHF1ZXN0aW9uIG1pZ2h0IG5v\r\ndCBiZSB2ZXJ5IGRpZmZpY3VsdCBidXQgc3RpbGwgcGxlYXNlIGhlbHAgbWUgb3V0LiBJIGhhdmUg\r\nMiB0eXBlcyBvZiBhcnJpdmFscyBmaWdodGluZyBmb3IgdGhlIHNhbWUgcmVzb3VyY2UuIEkgdHJp\r\nZWQgcGxvdHRpbmcgdGhlIHRvdGFsIHF1ZXVlIGxlbmd0aCB1c2luZyBzaW1tZXIucGxvdCB3aGlj\r\naCBpcyB3b3JraW5nLiBCdXQgaG93IGRvIEkgcGxvdCB0b3RhbCBudW1iZXIgb2YgZWFjaCBhcnJp\r\ndmFsIHR5cGUgaW4gdGhlIHF1ZXVlIG92ZXIgdGhlIGVudGlyZSB0aW1lIHBlcmlvZD8gSXMgdGhl\r\ncmUgYW55IGVsZWdhbnQgd2F5Pzxicj4KPGJyPgpFeGFtcGxlIDogQXQgYSB0aWNrZXQgY291bnRl\r\nciB0aGVyZSBhcmUgbWFsZXMgYW5kIGZlbWFsZXMgYXJyaXZpbmcgYXQgYSBkaWZmZXJlbnQgcmF0\r\nZS4gSSBhbSBhYmxlIHRvIHBsb3QgdGhlIHRvdGFsIHF1ZXVlIGxlbmd0aC4gQnV0IGhvdyB0byBJ\r\nIHBsb3QgdGhlIHRvdGFsIG51bWJlciBvZiBtYWxlcyBhbmQgZmVtYWxlcyBpbiB0aGUgcXVldWUg\r\nc2VwZXJhdGVseT88L2Jsb2NrcXVvdGU+PGJyPllvdSBjYW4gdXNlIGFkZGl0aW9uYWwgImR1bWIi\r\nIHJlc291cmNlcyB0byBhY2NvdW50IGZvciB0aGF0LiBFeGFtcGxlOjxicj48YnI+YGBgcjxicj5s\r\naWJyYXJ5KHNpbW1lcik8YnI+bGlicmFyeShzaW1tZXIucGxvdCk8YnI+PGJyPnBlcnNvbiAmbHQ7\r\nLSBmdW5jdGlvbihzZXgsIGxhbWJkYSk8YnI+Jm5ic3A7IHRyYWplY3RvcnkoKSA